   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Aki,<br><br>On the models that work, all K&#39;s are less than 0.5. It looks like the model that&#39;s failing is returning NA&#39;s for the three values on only one data point, and that the likelihood estimates for that data point are weirdly distributed in the model that&#39;s not working (see plots below). I&#39;m attaching the likelihood columns for this data point from the two models as well. Also tracking as an issue on GitHub: <a href=\"https://github.com/stan-dev/loo/issues/31\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/stan-dev/loo/issues/31&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792461010808000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0ZhbiRvcRh57MDJLF4f8wJ\">https://github.com/stan-dev/loo/issues/31</a><br><br>-Tor<br><p style=\"text-align:left;clear:both\"><a style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-DkPP-GhrxFA/V3UkhwQF2bI/AAAAAAAACGk/zw74szrsY5UeZPabMq2rIN-attATltRVgCLcB/s1600/doesnt_work.png\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-DkPP-GhrxFA/V3UkhwQF2bI/AAAAAAAACGk/zw74szrsY5UeZPabMq2rIN-attATltRVgCLcB/s1600/doesnt_work.png&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792461010808000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3b7Oe6FjyfIssonKd5eY6O\"><br></a></p><p style=\"text-align:left;clear:both\"><a style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-DkPP-GhrxFA/V3UkhwQF2bI/AAAAAAAACGk/zw74szrsY5UeZPabMq2rIN-attATltRVgCLcB/s1600/doesnt_work.png\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-DkPP-GhrxFA/V3UkhwQF2bI/AAAAAAAACGk/zw74szrsY5UeZPabMq2rIN-attATltRVgCLcB/s1600/doesnt_work.png&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792461010808000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3b7Oe6FjyfIssonKd5eY6O\"><br></a></p><p style=\"text-align:left;clear:both\"><a style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" href=\"https