onday, June 20, 2016 at 4:00:36 PM UTC+1, Tor Tarantola wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi all,<br><br>I&#39;m getting NA&#39;s when running LOO -- I haven&#39;t had this problem for other very similar models on the same data. I don&#39;t see any obvious differences between the likelihood matrices that worked and the one that didn&#39;t work (no zeros or NaNs). Any common causes I should check for? Unfortunately they&#39;re too large to attach (4,000 x 18,600).<br><br>Thanks as always.<br><br>Best,<br>Tor</div></blockquote></div></div></blockquote></div></blockquote></div>"
