    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br><br>On Thursday, June 30, 2016 at 4:30:26 PM UTC+1, Jonah Gabry wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small\">Ok, so the problem is that there is zero variance in the tail, i.e. all the values in the tail are the same. To see this you can do this in R: </span><div><br></div><div><div style=\"font-size:small\"><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">    log_lik </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> read</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">.</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">delim</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&quot;doesnt_work.txt&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> header</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">FALSE</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)[,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">2</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">]</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br>    log_weights </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">*</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> log_lik<br>    x </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">log_weights</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> max</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">log_weights</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">   </span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">    cutoff </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> quantile</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">x</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">0.8</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">  </span><span style=\"color:rgb(136,0,0)\"># find where the tail (20% largest values) starts</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,136)\">print</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">x</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">[</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">x </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> cutoff</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">])</span></div></font></code></div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\"><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\"><br></font></div></div></div></div></div></blockquote></div>"
    ]
